codex
All decisive gates now behave correctly: both positive claims close together with exit 0/`#Top`, two concrete K witness claims close, the fresh false result builds then fails on the actual `[]` residual, and changing the executed body from `+1` to `+2` builds then fails on `[0]` with the residual `[2]`. I’m consolidating the trust ledger and verdict; the remaining limitations are provenance records and the formal domain’s restriction to integer lists.
